.TH DECAF 1 "2026-09-29" "decaf" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
decaf \- suspend the system after a while
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B decaf
.I command
.RI [ argument ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B decaf
schedules a system suspend, using a transient
.BR systemd-run (1)
timer on the wall clock. When the timer fires, the system suspends even if
other programs hold inhibitor locks. It can be driven from the command line or
through a
.BR rofi (1)
menu.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI start " time"
Suspend after
.IR time .
A bare number is taken as minutes; units such as
.BR 90s ,
.BR 45m ,
.B 2h
or
.B 2h30m
are accepted. Starting again replaces the current timer.
.TP
.B stop
Cancel the timer.
.TP
.B status
Print the time left, or
.BR Inactive .
.TP
.B menu
Open the interactive rofi menu.
.TP
.BR version ", " \-\-version ", " \-V
Print the version.
.TP
.BR help ", " \-\-help ", " \-h
Print usage information.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
decaf start 30
decaf start 1h
decaf status
decaf stop
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemd-run (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR rofi (1)
.SH BUGS
Report issues at https://github.com/Davi-S/decaf/issues
